    pr_ref:  # 997a
    description: "Discovered 2026-05-31 during WI-kaziv bakeoff validation. Workaround: explicit --workdir pointing at the freshly-initialized broad-* session for cohort + cycle commands. Fix angle: change the sort key in resolve_workdir to extract the timestamp suffix (e.g., split on first '-' and sort by the rest), OR have each command filter by its own prefix. The _find_latest_session helper at line 446-462 already does prefix-filtering correctly — the bug is in resolve_workdir's auto-discover branch which accepts both prefixes."  # 997a
    fields:  # 997a
      statement: "scripts/bakeoff-broad resolve_workdir() (line ~432-441) scans the artifacts directory for sub-dirs starting with broad- OR deep-, sorts them lexicographically as full strings, and takes the last. Because d > b in ASCII, any deep-* directory always wins over any broad-* directory regardless of the timestamp suffix. A freshly-initialized broad-20260531-022124 session is silently superseded by a 3-week-old deep-20260510-054430 session."  # 997a
      root_cause: "Lexicographic sort over full directory names mixes the (prefix, timestamp) lexical order. Should sort by timestamp suffix only, or filter by prefix matching the current command expected mode."  # 997a
